### `me` as a Decimal, rounded to 34 digits (a tie as {Decimal} rounds one) when it has more.
### :returns: The decimal.
routine U256.to[Decimal]() -> Decimal
    return Decimal.of(dec_of_integer(neg: false, magnitude: me, f: decimal_format()))

### The integer part of `me`, toward zero, as an S8.
### :returns: The integer.
### :throws: Throws `IntegerOverflowError` when its integer part doesn't fit S8.
failable routine Decimal.to[S8]() -> S8
    part: DecInt = when check dec_int_part(me.dec())
        is DecInt as p => p
    return when check part.to_s256().to[S8]()
        is S8 as v => v

